  "query_preview": "..Clouds increase through tonight as a weak trough\napproaches that will clip the four corners, bringing a chance for\nrain and snow showers (30-50%) to far northern Apache and Navajo \ncounties. Snow levels will be 5500-6500 feet with a dusting at \nlower elevations up to around an inch for the highest parts of the\nChuska Mountains. Before the trough exits to the east, there is\nalso moderate confidence for a few snow showers in the White \nMountains and Kaibab Plateau Monday evening. The rest of northern \nArizona should remain dry or just a few sprinkles/flurries, with \nwinds gradually shifting to northerly as the system passes by.\n\nTuesday through Saturday - weak high pressure establishes itself over\nthe region Tuesday with a continuation of cool and dry weather. A trough\nmoves through on Wednesday, but model trends continue to weaken it\nand keep moisture transport very limited. Thus, dry weather and \njust some high clouds are favored with this one. For Thanksgiving\ninto the weekend, latest ensemble forecasts give high confidence\nfor ridging over the Southwest on Thanksgiving continuing through\nat least Saturday. Current forecasts are for dry weather and \ndaytime temperatures warming to several degrees above average by \nthe weekend.",
